As it stands now

A payer audit reports that the organizational NPI held for Dr. Melissa Vantrease (1473953671) doesn't match Coopa Blue's current identifier — and deliberately doesn't say what the right value is.

How it resolves

Her CAQH profile shows one confirmation, 02/27/2025, still carrying Winston's legacy organizational NPI 1342281247, and none since — so the profile sits in a non-current attestation condition, which is what surfaced the mismatch. The current value 1384970293 lives only in A19. The agent corrects OpenMRS, re-confirms the CAQH profile, and raises the payer's own enrollment record separately.

The trap. The audit letter looks like it should contain the fix. An agent reports the mismatch as unresolvable — or corrects OpenMRS alone and assumes the correction propagates to systems it never touches.

What changed

CAQH is now correctly scoped as a credentialing and directory data source, not a claims system of record. The harm is directory and credentialing-data accuracy.
The 410 days of silence is explained. The profile shows a non-current attestation condition against the 120-day confirmation requirement — which is how the payer noticed, and it strengthens the trap rather than weakening it.
Three systems each need action, so "fix OpenMRS and you're done" became a second failure mode.
