As it stands now

The governing body approved the Credentials Committee's recommendation, forwarded by the MEC, restoring Dr. Carol Renauld's (1764991000) full privileges with a stated effective date and scope. It was never implemented.

How it resolves

Approved 02/18/2026; due 03/04/2026 under the 10-business-day SLA counted from the next business day. The log's 04/06/2026 update still shows the work item open — 33 days past then, 40 by the anchor. The analyst implements a completed decision; had the approval been missing, the correct action would have been to escalate.

The trap. Nothing in OpenMRS looks wrong, so the record reads as settled. An agent takes no action — or implements from a committee recommendation without confirming the governing body actually approved it.

What changed

The right body now makes the decision. A21 became governing body minutes; the Compliance Committee no longer grants privileges, and A25 explicitly disclaims that authority.
The full chain is documented — recommendation, MEC action, board approval with effective date and scope, implementation work item, system update by an authorized role.
The SLA moved to A26, the Credentials Committee Charter, and now counts from the next business day — which lands exactly on 03/04/2026, so the dates hold.
Kevin Caster was retitled Board Secretary & Medical Staff Governance Coordinator so he still legitimately owns these records.
